d 'NNLME': module to estimate Nested Nonlinear Longitudinal Mixed-Effects regression
d
d     nnlme defines a program designed to implement a nested
d nonlinear regression following	a standard exponentiated
d survival curve. When working correctly, the program	    
d isolates a latent curve along which there is an exogenous but
d unobserved	    acceleration in the negative direction in the
d rate of change over time. Because time	is the main
d boundary defining parameter of interest, it is required for
d analysis to	     be feasible. 
d
d KW: panel data
d KW: mixed effects
d KW: nested models
d
d Requires: Stata version 17
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260730
d
d Author: Sean Clouston,  Stony Brook University
d Support: email Sean.Clouston@@stonybrookmedicine.edu
d
f nnlme.ado
f nnlme.sthlp
